<title>CHINA: Shanghai Metal Exchange closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Metal Exchange closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Metal Exchange was closed on Monday because of a National Day holiday, an exchange spokesman said. Trading will resume on Thursday, he said.</p>
<p>On Friday, the last trading day, the key copper three-month December 1996 contract closed up 130 yuan at 20,150 yuan per tonne and three-month aluminium did not trade.</p>
</text>
